  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the right triangle and the given information.\nThe triangle DEF is a right triangle with the right angle at E. We are given that DE is the hypotenuse and EF is one of the legs, with a length of 7 units. We are also given that $\\sin D = 0.7$.\n\nStep 2: Use the definition of sine in a right triangle.\nIn a right triangle, the sine of an angle is the ratio of the length of the opposite side to the length of the hypotenuse. Here, $\\sin D = \\frac{EF}{DE}$. Given that $\\sin D = 0.7$, we can write:\n\\[\n\\sin D = \\frac{7}{DE} = 0.7\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Solve for DE.\nRearrange the equation to solve for DE:\n\\[\nDE = \\frac{7}{0.7} = 10\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{10}<|im_end|>",
